  "worked_solution": "From the graph, we see that\n\n- The slope of the tangent at $x=-2$ is zero, so ${f}^{\u2032}(-2)=0.$\n\n- The slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is positive, so ${f}^{\u2032}(2)>0.$\n\n- The slope of the tangent at $x=5$ is negative, so ${f}^{\u2032}(5)<0.$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{\u2032}(5)<{f}^{\u2032}(-2)<{f}^{\u2032}(2).$",
